1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
And now it's the old scout master.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:16,600
Hey, we had a live chat this past week one morning for an hour or two, and the penguin

3
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,640
story came up again,

4
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:23,520
And so I haven't mentioned it in a long, long time.

5
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,880
So here's the penguin joke. okay,

6
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:26,960
We ready.

7
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:32,000
Two penguins are paddling a canoe through the Sahara Desert.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,520
The penguin in front turns to the penguin in the back of the canoe and says: where's your

9
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:36,520
paddle?

10
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:40,880
The penguin in the back of the canoe says: yep, it sure does.

11
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:46,680
Okay, discuss amongst yourselves.

12
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,800
This is podcast number 354..

13
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:49,800
Hey,

14
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:19,440
Welcome back to the Scout Master Podcast.

15
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:26,240
This is Clark Green with another non-standard podcast. but that's just the way this is

16
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:27,240
working right now.

17
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:29,040
I hope you don't mind.

18
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:33,480
Last week I published a post about girls in the BSA

19
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:39,200
And this was intended to be simple, to boil things down to, you know, the real kind

20
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:45,760
of crux of the issue, to share my point of view and how that point of view developed.

21
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:51,640
And in the post I talked about that because what I was talking about was our first trip

22
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:53,960
to Kandersteg International Scout Center.

23
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:58,160
Pardon me, if you've heard me, if I'm repeating myself, but Kandersteg International

24
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,800
Scout Center is in Switzerland.

25
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:01,760
You go there during the summer.

26
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:06,000
You're there with three or four hundred scouts from all over the world in many

27
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,800
different scouting organizations,

28
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:13,480
And the interesting thing that we were going to encounter in our first trip there

29
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:18,799
in 2011 was the fact that most of the rest of the world is scouting as co-ed.

30
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:24,399
So I was kind of curious about how that would work and what and how my

31
00:02:24,399 --> 00:02:27,600
scouts would react to it and how I would react to it myself.

32
00:02:27,959 --> 00:02:31,040
It wasn't totally sold on this being a very good idea.

33
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,239
I had my concerns, in other words.

34
00:02:33,679 --> 00:02:35,519
So we got to Kandersteg.

35
00:02:35,519 --> 00:02:38,600
It took my scouts a very brief period of time,

36
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:42,079
Of course. they and the scouts, you know, as they got out and about,

37
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:45,920
started meeting scouts from all over the world and and and saw that girls

38
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:50,640
and boys were in scouts together, you know, on the, exactly the same

39
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:52,400
organization, on the same footing.

40
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,400
They shared patrols,

41
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,400
They shared troops.

42
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:56,520
They thought it was novel and unusual,

43
00:02:56,520 --> 00:03:01,280
And then they just immediately accepted the idea that a scout is a scout.

44
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,800
I didn't even hear him discuss it all that much.

45
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:07,480
It took me slightly longer than them to get that idea

46
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:11,240
And it really was that simple.

47
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:12,440
Here it is:

48
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:13,760
Here's co-ed scouting.

49
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:14,760
It seems to work.

50
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:16,080
It seems to work fine,

51
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:19,400
And in the discussions I've had with scouts from other parts of the

52
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:25,360
world who are in a co-ed scouting organization, and some of them

53
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:30,640
that were there during the time that the organization went from

54
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:34,320
single sex to co-ed, when I've asked them about their experiences

55
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:37,680
and things, they don't seem to be all that different from the

56
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:41,760
experiences that I have had, just that there happened to be girls involved.

57
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:46,080
So I want to say again: it really is just that simple.

58
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,200
That's my thinking.

59
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,720
That's the way that this evolved.

60
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,280
It was that simple.

61
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,880
Hey, this seems to work,

62
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:52,880
Why not,

63
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:54,080
Let's go for it.

64
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:56,280
It's not political correctness,

65
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:59,000
It's not a feminist agenda, whatever that is.

66
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:04,080
It's just the way that my personal thinking changed on the idea.

67
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:07,200
I'm going to talk about how folks responded to the post.

68
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:12,120
Some of the things that they were concerned about cited organizational

69
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:14,520
issues and more on that later on.

70
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:18,000
It's not that I wasn't thinking about those things.

71
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:22,600
I just decided that they were unimportant and they clouded the discussion

72
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:28,280
And what I wanted to do was get things down to a very basic question,

73
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:33,560
And that question is: should gender define scouting and should gender

74
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:37,280
define our children's opportunities and futures?

75
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:39,680
I think that's the question we need to answer,

76
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:41,760
So let's focus on that for a moment.

77
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:45,440
We get confused easily, especially if you're my age.

78
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:51,280
I'm going to be referring to my age several times probably in this discussion,

79
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:53,880
So let me tell you: I'm 57 years old.

80
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:58,720
I know that we get confused sometimes or we use interchangeably

81
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:00,560
the term sex and gender.

82
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:04,640
Sex refers to the biological difference between males and females,

83
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:07,680
So that's chromosome and reproductive organs and hormones.

84
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,880
That's biological differences.

85
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:15,680
Gender refers to the cultural differences and roles that we impose

86
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:21,880
on and expect of men and women according to those biological differences.

87
00:05:22,159 --> 00:05:24,960
So I'm using the term gender here advisedly.

88
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,880
Biology is something we're born with.

89
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:29,800
Gender is something that we learned.

90
00:05:30,599 --> 00:05:31,640
Let me say that again:

91
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:34,039
Biology is something that we're born with.

92
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:40,520
The gender roles and expectations that we have is something that we learn

93
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:46,159
Now. if you feel uncomfortable talking about gender now,

94
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:48,840
you're really not going to like the next 20 years.

95
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:51,560
I mean, this is a high profile subject.

96
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:56,080
It's hotly politicized and there are very strong opinions about it.

97
00:05:56,200 --> 00:06:00,320
Some of what I'm talking about today is in the political sphere

98
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:05,880
of things right now, but let's not get distracted from the very simple question.

99
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:07,680
I'll repeat the simple question again:

100
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:12,120
Should gender define scouting and should gender define our children's

101
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:13,600
opportunities and futures?

102
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:16,680
My answer to that question is no. gender should not determine

103
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:18,680
our children's opportunities and futures.

104
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:20,120
It should not define scouting.

105
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:25,360
So I'm in favor of the idea that the BSA, the organization

106
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:28,440
that I'm a part of, should welcome girls as members.

107
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:35,280
Now, not everybody agreed with me, and that was no big surprise, as I expected,

108
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,480
You know. so let's take a look at the nature of the disagreements

109
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:40,360
and see what they bring to the discussion.

110
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:47,120
If you want to break it down in metrics, 45% of the responses

111
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:48,720
I received were absolutely positive-

112
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:52,080
Yes, I agree that this is a step forward that we should take.

113
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:57,159
37% of the responses I received were absolutely negative-

114
00:06:57,360 --> 00:07:04,120
No way, and 18% thought that it was probably a good idea, but they had

115
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:07,680
some sort of concern about making it happen or some sort of caveat

116
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:10,200
that they wanted to impose if we were to do this.

117
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:14,680
Now, more than half of the negative responses were reasonably respectful.

118
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:20,720
The other half were kind of dismissive and were like about things

119
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:25,040
that weren't really related to the things I had been discussing in the post.

120
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:28,280
So I had to wonder if they had really read about it at all.

121
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:34,880
A very diminishing few of the negative responses were just downright mean

122
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:40,360
and nasty or profane and I excluded them from comments on the post

123
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:42,560
or I hid those comments on Facebook.

124
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,840
The Scouters are usually very good folks

125
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:49,880
And even if, when we disagree, they can speak respectfully to someone

126
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:51,720
rather than speaking past them.

127
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:57,640
So there was a very, very few instances where people were kind of out of line.

128
00:07:57,840 --> 00:08:01,640
So, as far as the disagreements go, I think it's safe to divide them

129
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:05,920
into two broad categories, the first being organizational issues

130
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:08,360
and the second being gender related issues.

131
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:11,160
So let's talk about the organizational issues first.

132
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:13,880
Now, everybody who's listening to this is probably the member

133
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:17,360
of a scouting organization, but we have to keep reminding ourselves

134
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:20,160
that organizations are not scouting.

135
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:24,000
The worldwide scouting movement is something bigger and broader

136
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:28,680
and more important than any organizational structure that purports the containant.

137
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,040
What do I mean by that?

138
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:36,560
Well, the BSA, the Girl Scouts, the Girl Guides, the World Organization,

139
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:40,960
the Scouting Movement, any national organization is an organization

140
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:47,320
that, while it promotes and enables people to have scouting,

141
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:48,920
it's not scouting itself.

142
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:52,280
And that distinction becomes important in this kind of a discussion,

143
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:57,760
because we don't want to make a decision about this based on what's best for the organization.

144
00:08:57,760 --> 00:09:02,439
We want to make a decision about this: what's best for young people.

145
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:05,760
So I'm all about getting things into single sentences,

146
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:11,400
And if I want to get my work as a scouter into a single sentence

147
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:17,120
that is as simple as possible, it would be this: that is, to give young people

148
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:19,440
in my community the opportunity to be scouts.

149
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:21,040
That's my whole job,

150
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:22,440
That's what I do.

151
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:24,880
So there are things that are going to help me do this

152
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:26,960
and things that are going to stand in my way.

153
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:30,600
If the organization I'm part of is standing in the way of that mission,

154
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:34,280
I need to consider whether or not I want to remain a part of that organization

155
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:37,000
If that organization isn't going to change.

156
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:43,280
Now organizations have to be kind of impenetrable and inflexible.

157
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,600
I like to think of them like ships.

158
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:50,920
OK, so these organizations are ships and the ocean is the culture

159
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:53,720
and the society and the world that we're living in,

160
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:56,880
And organizations need to be safe and stable,

161
00:09:57,280 --> 00:10:00,640
And that's this you know, and that's important for ships too.

162
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:02,520
So they're fairly rigid.

163
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:07,400
You don't want the ocean inside your ship because that's not going to work very well.

164
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:12,400
So to stay afloat over all this, they have to be this way.

165
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:17,680
And that impenetrability and inflexibility creates a lot of drag,

166
00:10:17,959 --> 00:10:20,400
especially when it comes to evolution and change,

167
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:24,439
And this drag is commensurate with the size and the scope of the organization.

168
00:10:24,439 --> 00:10:28,280
The bigger the ship, the longer it takes to turn right.

169
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:32,959
The ocean of culture is, of course, much wider and deeper and more fluid

170
00:10:33,319 --> 00:10:37,400
and changeable than the organizational ships that travel over them.

171
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:41,760
So scouting organizations usually embrace change very slowly.

172
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:46,480
individual scouts and scouts can embrace change very quickly.

173
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:51,439
Any organization of national scope and a century and more than a century

174
00:10:51,439 --> 00:10:55,880
of service is going to be likely to have found itself behind the curve

175
00:10:56,319 --> 00:10:57,840
from time to time.

176
00:10:57,840 --> 00:11:01,960
Big national organizations are often kind of reluctant to face

177
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:07,319
cultural realities, especially when they are championing a set of values

178
00:11:07,319 --> 00:11:10,800
and ethics that are supposed to be unchangeable and unauthorable.

179
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:16,120
But but scouting organizations have changed how they interpret

180
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:18,480
and express their values many, many times.

181
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:23,160
Some of these changes were motivated internally, some by external pressure,

182
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:27,800
And you can't adjust your core principles based on petitions

183
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:32,920
or leaving them up to a majority vote. but you can evolve right.

184
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:35,560
You can evolve in the way that you express them,

185
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:39,320
And that means making changes, and change is not all bad.

186
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:44,560
So what should be important to us as scouts is following the best ethical

187
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:47,600
and moral path. if that means change, then we change,

188
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:51,640
Then we sort out how the organization handles the change.

189
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:55,040
We can't begin with the idea of protecting the organization right.

190
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:57,640
We have to get the ethics and morals right.

191
00:11:57,640 --> 00:12:02,440
So that's why arguments over whether this is best for the BSA organizationally,

192
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:06,320
or if it will hurt the girl scouts, or this idea that

193
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:11,200
the only reason that girls want to become boy scouts is because girl scouts

194
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:13,040
isn't up to snuff,

195
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:17,280
So let's change girl scouts instead of allowing girls to come into boy scouts-

196
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:21,080
All of those issues don't touch the central, simple question

197
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:24,920
And I really am past worrying about them.

198
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:27,280
And I don't mean that to be dismissive,

199
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:29,440
I don't mean that to sound snarky,

200
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:32,880
But you know I think I explain myself reasonably well.

201
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:38,439
The answers to this question can't be decided on issues of organizational

202
00:12:38,439 --> 00:12:39,600
imperatives alone

203
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:44,880
And to my mind organizational imperatives are unimportant when it

204
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:46,320
comes to answering this question.

205
00:12:46,560 --> 00:12:50,760
So the other chief objections came from gender issues,

206
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:55,760
The idea that boys and girls and men and women are so basically

207
00:12:55,760 --> 00:13:01,160
different from each other that they must have their own safe spaces

208
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:04,520
to express those differences apart from each other.

209
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:09,760
And one often repeated idea in the people who don't think girls should

210
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:15,079
be a part of the BSA was that boys will find the girls so distracting,

211
00:13:15,079 --> 00:13:18,959
that they can't- quote- be themselves around girls.

212
00:13:20,199 --> 00:13:23,839
There was also the idea that boys could not compete with girls

213
00:13:23,839 --> 00:13:25,560
who mature faster than boys.

214
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:30,880
And then some very few asserted this idea of a war

215
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:36,160
on boys and that boys were no longer allowed to behave as boys

216
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:38,800
And they were being over feminized by schools

217
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:42,480
And you know a lot of things. that kind of started to encroach

218
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:46,000
on the political arena, that they're no longer allowed to express

219
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:49,920
boy behavior, whatever that is, and that they're being made

220
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:52,280
ashamed of themselves for being boys,

221
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:54,960
And these were usually pretty strident objections.

222
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:58,920
I did say that the negative reactions to this are fairly predictable,

223
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:01,880
because when you take a privileged group of people and you say,

224
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:04,680
well, you should probably think about letting other people

225
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:09,640
enjoy these privileges to, it feels like an attack. you know,

226
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:10,680
and I understand that,

227
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:12,840
I really do understand that

228
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:15,200
It wasn't really meant to be snarky.

229
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:19,320
It was like, OK, I understand that when you hear this

230
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:24,280
proposal, that you're going to look on it as an attack

231
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:27,600
coming from the outside. but it's not. it's not.

232
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:29,600
I'm not on the outside.

233
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:34,160
I've been a BSA volunteer for like 35 years and this,

234
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:37,440
No, this is not an outside attack.

235
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:40,760
This is an honest proposal that we could probably be a better

236
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:43,920
organization if we looked at taking this way forward.

237
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:49,760
But back to these gender issues. OK, nobody specified what precisely

238
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:56,320
behavior or expressions boys can only develop amongst themselves

239
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:58,360
when girls are not present.

240
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:02,760
I can't think of one positive behavior or one positive self image

241
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:08,240
or one ethical or moral ideal that meets that definition.

242
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:13,440
What can't boys express that's a positive self image,

243
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:15,960
that's good behavior, that's ethical and moral,

244
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:19,320
only amongst themselves, without girls present?

245
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:21,680
I don't understand what that would be.

246
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:23,680
I can't think of one thing-

247
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:25,800
And if you can, let me know,

248
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:29,240
But I really can't think of one positive thing

249
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:33,240
that boys can only express when girls aren't around,

250
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:35,440
And I'm going to say this to there.

251
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:37,440
I want to make this very clear.

252
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:41,040
There are a lot of things that I, at my age,

253
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:45,800
have learned about being a man that I have had to unlearn

254
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:47,960
and I've had to reject,

255
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:50,440
And I think there's a lot of things that women my age

256
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:53,080
were conditioned to do and accept about themselves

257
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:55,560
that they have had to overcome.

258
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:59,760
So people my age have not necessarily found

259
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:01,840
the gender conditioning we received as children

260
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,960
to be absolutely positive,

261
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:06,800
And as scouts we should not perpetuate

262
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:09,800
any of these negative gender stereotypes.

263
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:11,840
We're in the character building business,

264
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:14,920
And I think we can skip over the idea

265
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:18,080
that women of good character and men of good character

266
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:20,520
are some fundamentally different kind of thing

267
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:23,760
that can only develop in gender specific environments

268
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:26,400
and say that we can do this together.

269
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:30,400
So we want to develop young people of good character.

270
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:33,920
So the other branch of the gender based issues

271
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:38,200
that were used as a counter argument to my proposal

272
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:42,560
was 11 to 16 year old. girls are more mature than boys

273
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:44,080
and boys don't have a fighting chance

274
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:46,000
to take on leadership opportunities.

275
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:49,319
Some people said a completely different thing:

276
00:16:49,319 --> 00:16:51,600
that the boys would run rough shot over the girls

277
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:54,480
and everything, And I don't think either case is true.

278
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:57,840
But even if they were true, it wouldn't change my answer

279
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,600
to the simple question we started with:

280
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:03,160
Should gender define our children's opportunities

281
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:05,040
and futures? No, it shouldn't.

282
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:08,319
So what I didn't want to do with this post-

283
00:17:08,319 --> 00:17:10,839
and I think that clouds the issues-

284
00:17:10,839 --> 00:17:13,400
try and turn it into some kind of an academic discussion,

285
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:16,360
citing and counter, citing articles and studies

286
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:18,720
and things like that, because there are plenty of studies out there.

287
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:20,640
There are plenty of articles out there

288
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:24,680
that will give you adequate fodder to have long debates

289
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:27,720
about the influence of gender conditioning

290
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:29,760
in the way that we treat boys and girls,

291
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:32,560
the negative and positive aspects of that,

292
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:35,400
and the difference between how gender and biology

293
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:38,560
define our opportunities and choices and futures.

294
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:42,960
But I want to return to the one simple question:

295
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:46,080
Should scouting be defined by gender

296
00:17:46,199 --> 00:17:50,040
and should gender define our children's

297
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:52,040
opportunities and their futures?

298
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:54,600
I think the very clear answer is no.

299
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:57,280
Gender should not define our children's

300
00:17:57,280 --> 00:17:58,919
opportunities and futures

301
00:17:58,919 --> 00:18:01,800
And I think that a coed atmosphere

302
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:03,840
when they're in these developmental years

303
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:07,480
would be a very positive and important thing to have in scouting

304
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:10,120
to better serve the youth in our communities.

305
00:18:10,199 --> 00:18:13,120
I'm fine with people having a different opinion about that.

306
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:14,680
I'm fine with them.

307
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:16,880
I'm fine with chartered organizations

308
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:19,960
being able to choose whether they want to be fully coed,

309
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:22,800
where they want to have kind of a separate

310
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:26,680
but equal program going on, where there's some separation

311
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:28,840
in the genders, or whether they just want to continue

312
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:31,160
on and have a single sex organization,

313
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:34,160
whether it be boys or girls, and then let families

314
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:37,040
make the choice of what unit they want to be a part of.

315
00:18:37,040 --> 00:18:38,960
Don't think it causes a great deal of trouble.

316
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:41,200
Don't think it makes a big problem for anybody.

317
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:44,080
So there's no doubt going to be some reaction

318
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:46,800
to the podcast, both negative and positive,

319
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:48,240
And that's fine.

320
00:18:48,240 --> 00:18:50,160
This is a good discussion to have

321
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:54,600
And scouts are pretty good at having respectful conversations

322
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:57,360
about issues over which we disagree.

323
00:18:57,720 --> 00:19:01,240
But remember the single, simple question:

324
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:04,480
Should gender define scouting

325
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:07,760
and should gender define our children's

326
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:09,640
opportunities and futures?

327
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:11,960
That's the question that we have to answer.

328
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:14,320
All the other organizational imperatives

329
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:16,360
and things like that are not as important

330
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,440
as answering that single question

331
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:20,440
in an ethical and a moral sense.

332
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,640
Thank you for listening today.

333
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:24,720
I really appreciate you tuning in.

334
